# ── Derived data: regenerable, and not version controlled ─────────────

# The market-data cache. Fetched from the source; deleting it refetches.
.cache/

# **The leading slash is required.** Without it, `research/` matches a directory of
# that name at any depth and excludes the whole `backtest/research/` code package —
# with `git status` clean, `git add -A` raising nothing, and no trace at all. That
# happened: six research modules were never published while their tests were, and a
# fresh clone crashed. tools/check_shipped.py now guards against it.
#
# Your research record: run history, trade logs, notes.
# **This is your local asset, not code.** Why it is not committed:
#   1. SQLite is binary; a few runs on two machines conflict and cannot be merged
#   2. It holds judgements and process, not a reproducible artefact — someone else
#      cloning and rerunning would get their own
# To back it up, copy this directory on its own.
/research/

# Backtest exports
out/

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ── Editors and the OS ────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
